# Spec 022 — Norway car total-cost-of-ownership module (engine, market model, core screens)

Status: Draft
Owner: <you>
Related: 006-deployment (single container, committed data), 004-backend-hardening
(rate limits, health probe), 009-zip-explorer (shareable URL state), 021-production-token-guard
(fixture vs live reporting). Source documents: the owner's MVP build spec
(Claude Doc "Norway car TCO app — MVP build spec") and the six wireframes
("Norway car TCO app — wireframes": Main, Market, Results, ResultsCurves,
Detail, Checklist).

## Overview

A second product surface inside LiveNear, at `/cars`, for people moving to
Norway: which car, got which way (buy new, lease, used 1–3 years, used 5+
years), costs least for the time they will actually keep it, and how sure
that answer is. Every number shows its source, its date and whether it is an
estimate. Decision support, not financial advice.

This spec covers milestones M0–M3 of the owner's build spec: the skeleton,
the pure cost engine, the market model v1 with its ingestion core, and the
four core screens (Your situation, Compare table, Compare curves, Option
detail). The market map, the newcomer checklist, automated price-list and
lease pulls, the quarantine review view and the weekly unattended run are
follow-up specs (023+).

## Context

- LiveNear has no database, no accounts and persists no personal data
  (CLAUDE.md). The car module keeps that: a user's situation, selection,
  overrides and checklist ticks live in the browser (`localStorage`) and in
  one compact URL parameter, exactly as the map's share links do (009 R5).
  Scenario runs are stateless requests.
- Data follows the housing convention (001, 007): derived, small, versioned
  artefacts are committed under `backend/data/cars/` and shipped in the
  image. Private inputs (hand-collected listings, raw fetched pages) never
  enter the public repo; they live in the owner's Cloudflare R2 bucket and
  are read at startup when credentials are present, with a synthetic fixture
  otherwise (same shape as the isochrone fixture, 021).
- FINN.no's `robots.txt` ("Crawling FINN.no is prohibited unless you have
  written permission", checked 2026-10-31) and user terms §6 forbid
  automated or systematic collection without explicit written consent. The
  module builds **no FINN scraper** and uses no third-party scraping service
  for FINN. Used-car data enters through a CSV importer (hand-collected by
  the owner) until FINN grants consent in writing; the request is drafted in
  `backend/docs/cars/finn-consent-request.md`. This keeps CLAUDE.md's hard
  constraint intact.
- Stack additions are deliberate and small: `numpy` + `pyyaml` (+ optional
  `boto3`) in the web image; `statsmodels`, `scipy`, `pandas`, `hypothesis`
  for the offline fit and tests; `playwright`, `selectolax`, `pdfplumber`
  for ingestion only. Frontend adds `react-router-dom` and five d3
  micro-packages (scale, shape, array, brush, selection) for the charts;
  no UI kit, no query library.

## Requirements

### Skeleton and state

- **R1 — Module layout and routing.** Backend code lives in
  `backend/app/cars/` (`engine/`, `market/`, `ingest/`, `rules/`,
  `schemas.py`, `data_bundle.py`) with one router at `/api/cars/*`
  registered before the SPA mount. Frontend code lives in
  `frontend/src/cars/` with routes `/cars` (situation), `/cars/compare`,
  `/cars/compare/curves`, `/cars/option/:optionId`; `/` stays the map. The
  backend serves `index.html` for any non-`/api` path so deep links reload.
  CLAUDE.md and README gain a Cars section (commands, data rules,
  attribution); the existing hard constraints are unchanged.
- **R2 — Browser-held profile.** The profile (exit odds over 1/2/3/4+
  years, km per year, charging mix, home municipality, cash or loan, return
  on cash, down payment, insurance profile, limits, fun weight, preferred
  cost measure), the market selection and any overrides are typed, saved
  under `livenear.cars.*` in `localStorage`, and round-trip through a single
  URL parameter `c` (base64url JSON, defaults omitted). No request stores
  them server-side; no cookie or identifier is set.

### Engine

- **R3 — Line items and measures.** A pure package (no I/O, no clock, no
  network; dates and seeds are inputs) computes, per option, a monthly
  schedule from month 0 to 60: cash flows (purchase or down payment, fees,
  upfront rent, re-registration, winter tyres, delay cost at month 0; loan
  or lease payments, insurance, traffic-insurance tax, energy, tyres by km,
  service thereafter) and exit terms as functions of the exit month (resale
  value, loan payoff, lease early-exit charge, excess-km fee, exit
  friction). From these it derives all five measures at every month:
  total cost of ownership, net present cost, net cost per month (default),
  cash up front and cost per km, following the build spec's formulas
  (opportunity cost only in undiscounted measures). Expected value of each
  measure is Σ p(t)·measure(t) over the user's exit odds, computed per
  measure; best and worst are the extremes over exit points with p(t) > 0.
  Deterministic amounts are integer øre; rounding happens only for display.
- **R4 — Uncertainty bands.** 2,000 seeded Monte Carlo draws per option,
  drawing resale from the market model's predictive distribution and
  insurance, loan rate and charging prices from ranges in the inputs,
  report P10/P50/P90 for every measure at every month. The same seed gives
  byte-identical results; adding an option does not change another
  option's draws. Ten options run in under 2 s on a laptop. With all ranges
  collapsed, the P50 path equals the integer deterministic path exactly.
- **R5 — Provenance and status.** Every input carries id, value, source,
  as-of date, status (Live or Estimate) and, for defaults, a written basis.
  Every line item lists the input ids it used. An option is Live only when
  every input above a materiality threshold (share of expected TCO flowing
  through items that used it) is Live. No silent defaults: every default is
  Estimate with its basis in the inputs file.
- **R6 — Tax rules file.** Traffic-insurance tax, re-registration fee and
  the EV VAT rule live only in `backend/app/cars/rules/tax_rules.yaml`, each
  entry with `effective_from`, `effective_to`, parameters and `source_url`.
  Lookup by date selects exactly one rule or raises. Months beyond the last
  dated rule carry it forward flagged Estimate. The reported EV VAT
  threshold change for 2027 is recorded as `status: unverified` and not
  applied until an official source is cited.

### Market model and ingestion

- **R7 — Market model v1.** Cohort = variant (trim group from Vegvesen
  battery, drive and power) × model year, with hand-maintained mid-year
  splits. Per-cohort robust log-price regression on log km, slopes shrunk
  toward the segment mean in proportion to sample size (empirical Bayes,
  statsmodels), global dealer / fleet / warranty terms (fixed, documented
  priors flagged Estimate where unidentifiable). Cohorts with fewer than 5
  listings are Estimate. Predictive intervals are for a single car. Retention
  curves r(age, km) per model pooled by segment come from cohort values
  divided by the owner-supplied new-price history (CPI and VAT adjusted);
  market drift defaults to 0 with a cited range until 12 weekly snapshots
  exist. A backtest (fit to week w, predict last ask of listings removed
  after w; leave-one-out CV until the removed set reaches 100) reports MAPE
  by segment and age plus 80 % interval coverage with a Wilson interval, and
  fails the build only when the coverage interval's upper bound is below
  70 %. The report renders for at least 4 models.
- **R8 — Ingestion core.** One runner (`python -m app.cars.ingest.runner`)
  walks fetch → parse → validate → reconcile → store for each enabled
  source: the listings CSV importer (column contract in the README), Statens
  vegvesen vehicle API (cached), Norges Bank and SSB open APIs, the Tesla
  configurator (Playwright; never from the web container), and manual lease
  quotes. Every raw response is stored with URL, timestamp and sha256 (to
  R2 under `raw/<source>/<date>/` when configured, else a gitignored local
  folder). Rows failing validation go to a quarantine file, never into the
  store; health checks fail the run on zero rows or an empty-rate jump; a
  2 % sample is queued for spot checks. Registration numbers and VINs are
  hashed before storage. Terms decisions per source, with dates, are logged
  in `backend/docs/cars/sources.md`. No FINN adapter exists.
- **R9 — Data bundle and fixture mode.** The fit writes a small derived
  bundle (`vehicles`, `cohorts`, `retention`, `new_prices`, `lease_offers`,
  `rates`, `meta` with as-of dates) to `backend/data/cars/`, loaded once at
  startup and cached. Listings behind a cohort point load from R2 when
  `CARS_R2_*` are set, otherwise from a committed synthetic fixture; the
  health probe reports `cars: {bundle_as_of, listings: "r2" | "fixture" |
  "unavailable"}`. Production without R2 credentials is reported, not
  papered over.

### API and screens

- **R10 — API.** JSON over HTTP with Pydantic models (OpenAPI):
  `GET /api/cars/vehicles`, `GET /api/cars/market/cohorts` (filters: make,
  year range, max price, energy type, must-haves), `GET
  /api/cars/market/cohorts/{id}/listings`, `POST /api/cars/scenarios`
  (profile + selection + overrides + seed → per option and month P10/P50/P90
  for every measure, expected/best/worst, line items at each exit, inputs
  with provenance, status, options ruled out by limits with reasons,
  sensitivity of the top option), `GET /api/cars/sources`. GETs use the
  data rate limit; the scenario POST has its own (`CARS_SCENARIO_LIMIT`,
  default 30/minute). No response contains a registration number, VIN or
  secret. What-if overrides are request data only.
- **R11 — Core screens.** Behaviour per the wireframes and build spec:
  - *Your situation*: four exit-odds percentages that must sum to 100 % (stacked
    bar; Continue blocked otherwise); limits are filters, never weighted.
  - *Compare — table*: one row per car × way to get it, ranked by the expected
    value of the selected measure; range bar from best to worst exit with the
    expected mark; fun score column; Live/Estimate badge per option; ruled-out
    options listed with reasons; sensitivity panel for the top option.
  - *Compare — curves*: x = years of ownership 0.5–5, y = selected measure;
    colour = car, line style = way to get it; P10–P90 bands toggleable; end
    labels with collision avoidance; exit-marker slider driving a ranking;
    what-if sliders (return on cash, loan rate, km per year, used-price
    drift, cash or loan) rerun with overrides, Save writes them to the
    profile, Reset restores it.
  - *Option detail*: tiles for expected, best exit, worst exit, cash up front;
    cost-by-exit chart against the best lease and best new option for the same
    model; line items as bars; inputs table with value, source, date, status
    and Override.
  - Shared: measure selector in both Compare views and Detail; NOK with a
    space thousands separator and `kr`; units on every header and axis;
    tooltips give source and date; works at phone width; every control is a
    real labelled input; contrast ≥ 4.5:1.
- **R12 — Tests.** At least six golden cases (new cash, new loan, lease,
  lease early exit, used 1–3 years from a dealer, used 5+ years private,
  excess km) as YAML input plus expected output with a worked example each,
  matching to the øre; the loan schedule matches a published amortisation
  example; Hypothesis properties: cumulative cash flows never fall;
  TCO excluding early-exit charges never falls when resale is
  non-increasing; more km never lowers TCO; a higher return on cash never
  lowers the TCO of a cash purchase; net present cost equals TCO when r = 0
  and opportunity cost is off; expected lies between best and worst;
  P10 ≤ P50 ≤ P90; same seed, same bytes; Σ display items = TCO. Market
  tests recover known parameters from synthetic data and hit ≈ 80 % coverage.
  Ingestion tests run parsers on stored fixtures and each validation rule
  on a failing fixture. Frontend tests cover the profile codec, the exit-odds
  gate, the measure switch, override and Save/Reset request bodies, NOK
  formatting and a flow across the four screens over a mocked API.

## Non-functional / Constraints

- No secrets in the frontend bundle; R2 credentials only in the backend
  environment (Render dashboard, GitHub Actions secrets).
- Web image stays small: no statsmodels, pandas or Playwright at runtime.
- Engine purity: `app/cars/engine` and `app/cars/market` import no I/O,
  clock or network modules; seeds are passed in.
- Money is integer øre in the engine and in stored data; floats appear only
  inside the Monte Carlo arrays and are converted back once.
- Tests before formulas: a golden case or property is added before a line
  item changes.
- Ask the owner before any paid service, hosted dependency or account.
- Norwegian UI is out of scope; English copy, nb-NO number formatting.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] R1: `/cars` and its sub-routes render inside the deployed SPA and
      survive a hard reload; `/` is unchanged; `pytest` and `npm run test`
      pass in CI with no changes to the existing jobs.
- [ ] R2: a profile encoded in `?c=` reproduces the same screens in a fresh
      tab; the backend logs and responses contain no profile fields.
- [ ] R3: `python -m app.cars.engine.cli backend/scenarios/<owner>.yaml`
      prints ranked options and line items; golden cases match to the øre.
- [ ] R4: scenario POST for 10 options × 2,000 draws completes in < 2 s on
      the fixture bundle; seed test passes; collapsed-range equality holds.
- [ ] R5: every input in the detail inputs table shows source, date and
      status; an option becomes Estimate when a material input is Estimate.
- [ ] R6: rule lookup tests pass; the 2027 VAT entry is `unverified` and not
      applied.
- [ ] R7: `backend/docs/cars/backtest.md` renders for ≥ 4 models with MAPE
      and coverage; thin cohorts are flagged; the coverage gate test exists.
- [ ] R8: an ingest run against the fixture CSV stores validated rows,
      quarantines the failing fixture rows, and fails loudly on an empty
      source; no module under `ingest/sources/` references finn.no.
- [ ] R9: `/api/health` reports `cars.bundle_as_of` and `listings` mode;
      without R2 the listings endpoint serves the fixture in dev and reports
      `unavailable` in production.
- [ ] R10: OpenAPI lists the endpoints; responses never contain a
      registration number or VIN (test).
- [ ] R11: the owner enters their situation, sees ranked options and curves,
      switches measure, moves every what-if slider, saves, resets, overrides
      an input and sees the rank update; phone-width layout stacks.
- [ ] R12: all listed tests exist and pass.

## Out of Scope (explicit)

- Market map screen with box-select, newcomer checklist screen, quarantine
  review UI, automated brand price lists and lease portals, the weekly
  GitHub Actions ingest PR, validation sign-off (follow-up specs 023+).
- Any FINN automation, including hosted scraping services.
- Accounts, payments, native apps, insurer or lender integrations,
  Norwegian UI, market model v2 (hierarchical Bayesian).

